#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=10 nAlgorithms=7;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version dev) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1786209248888'; [Sat Aug 08 19:14:08 CEST 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using RazorNet (version dev)  ((Huson and Bryant 2024) ;  The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods, 2024.), ((Hayamizu et al, 2026 ; M. Hayamizu, others, D.H. Huson, in preparation).
The original input consisted of 90 taxa and 90 DNA sequences of length 1,281.
The Razor Haplo Net method was used (default options, except MaxPolishRounds=1) so as to obtain 230 nodes and 339 edges.
The Median Joining method (Bandelt et al 1999) was used (default options) so as to obtain 121 nodes and 122 edges.

References:
(Hayamizu et al, 2026: M. Hayamizu, others, D.H. Huson, in preparation
(Huson and Bryant 2024):  The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods, 2024.
Bandelt et al 1999: HJ Bandelt, P. Forster, and A. Röhl. Median-joining networks for inferring intraspecific phylogenies. Molecular Biology and Evolution, 16:37–48, 1999.
]

